\~"There's a porpoise close behind us, and he's treading on my tail.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~See how eagerly the lobsters and the turtles all advance!\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~They are waiting on the shingle--will you come and join the dance?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, will you join the dance?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~Will you, won't you, will you, won't you, won't you join the dance?\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~"You can really have no notion how delightful it will be\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~When they take us up and throw us, with the lobsters, out to sea!"\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~But the snail replied "Too far, too far!" and gave a look askance--\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~Said he thanked the whiting kindly, but he would not join the dance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~Would not, could not, would not, could not, would not join the dance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~Would not, could not, would not, could not, could not join the dance.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~'"What matters it how far we go?" his scaly friend replied.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~"There is another shore, you know, upon the other side.\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
\~\par\pard\plain\hyphpar} {	
